Shared memory daemon (spec 0113 delta-02): defaulting copilot to HTTP.
  Without it, every session spawns its own memory server and only the
  first one to write can write — the rest are refused for their whole life.
  copilot now reaches shared memory through the daemon.

  NOTE: this run switched copilot only. Still on the previous arrangement:
    - claude
    - antigravity
  They will contend for the memory lock with copilot until they switch too.
  Switch the whole machine at once with: task mempalace:switch-http

  Restart any running copilot session to pick this up.
  MemPalace reaches shared memory through the HTTP daemon.

